# Normalise line endings at checkout, not in the repository, so that the same
# blob works on every platform someone builds PicoLM on.
#
# Why this file exists: tools/msvc_build.bat was committed with LF-only line
# endings. cmd.exe tolerates LF for simple commands, but its label lookup
# (goto :label / call :label) scans the file as a byte stream and mis-handles
# LF-only files, so the build died with
#
#   The system cannot find the batch label specified - parse_args
#
# before compiling anything. Every .bat here relies on goto/call labels, so
# they must be CRLF on disk regardless of what the repository stores.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.btm           text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts must stay LF, or the kernel refuses them (bad interpreter) and
# a CRLF-checked-out ./script.sh fails in a way that looks like a missing
# interpreter rather than a line-ending problem.
*.sh            text eol=lf
configure       text eol=lf

# Sources: let each platform's normal convention apply, so a checkout on
# Windows gets CRLF in the editor without changing what the compiler sees.
*.c             text
*.h             text
*.md            text
*.txt           text

# Binary-ish assets: never touch these.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.gguf          binary
*.o             binary
*.exe           binary
